  [   98.0-  102.5] quarter appears to have brought an even more rapid advance led by healthy
  [  102.5-  107.6] consumer spending likely running above 3 percent growth and business
  [  107.6-  114.7] investment likely rising at about a double-digit pace. Capital expenditures
  [  114.7-  120.9] are at a historically high share of GDP. High-tech investment is leading the
  [  120.9-  125.8] acceleration. But there's also been a broadening in other categories and these
  [  125.8-  131.2] trends bear watching. What about the jobless rate? The jobless rate is lower
  [  131.2-  137.7] than a year ago and payroll growth is noticeably above last year's pace. The
  [  137.7-  142.8] four-week moving average of unemployment insurance claims continues to run at
  [  142.8-  148.0] the lowest level in generations. So on the employment side of the Fed's dual
